{"command": "cd /testbed && cat specs/001-transactions/contracts/add-contract.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "# Contract: `add(a, b)` Function\n\n## Purpose\n\nDefine the interface contract for the `add(a, b)` function in `smoke.py`.\n\n## Interface\n\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Return the sum of two numeric arguments.\n    \n    Args:\n        a: First numeric operand (int or float).\n        b: Second numeric operand (int or float).\n    \n    Returns:\n        The sum of a and b. Type follows Python's native numeric promotion.\n    \n    Raises:\n        (Out of scope) TypeError if inputs are non-numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    return a + b\n```\n\n## Preconditions\n\n1. `a` must be an instance of `int` or `float`.\n2. `b` must be an instance of `int` or `float`.\n\n## Postconditions\n\n1. The return value equals `a + b` (Python's native addition).\n2. The return type follows Python's numeric promotion rules:\n   - `int + int` → `int`\n   - `int + float` → `float`\n   - `float + int` → `float`\n   - `float + float` → `float`\n\n## Test Cases (Contract Verification)\n\n| Test ID | Input (a, b) | Expected Output | Type |\n|---------|-------------|-----------------|------|\n| TC-01 | (2, 3) | 5 | int |\n| TC-02 | (1.5, 2.5) | 4.0 | float |\n| TC-03 | (2, 3.5) | 5.5 | float |\n| TC-04 | (0, 0) | 0 | int |\n| TC-05 | (0, 5) | 5 | int |\n| TC-06 | (-3, -7) | -10 | int |\n| TC-07 | (-3, 7) | 4 | int |\n| TC-08 | (7, -3) | 4 | int |\n| TC-09 | (-1.5, 2.5) | 1.0 | float |\n| TC-10 | (1000000, 2000000) | 3000000 | int |\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. `add(a, b) == add(b, a)` (commutativity)\n2. `add(a, 0) == a` (zero identity)\n3. `add(a, b) + c == a + add(b, c)` (associativity)\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- None. Pure function with no external dependencies.\n"}